WEBVTT

00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:08.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-sixth. Can everyone hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:15.259
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, got you. Nearly joined from the car. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid.</v>

00:00:17.269 --> 00:00:19.370
<v Tomasz Nowak>You and half the factory, then.</v>

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:25.289
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Honestly, ten minutes looking at the same bloke's brake lights.</v>

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:29.699
<v Tomasz Nowak>Still more entertaining than the football last night.</v>

00:00:30.309 --> 00:00:32.409
<v David Whitfield>Depends which end you were supporting.</v>

00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:38.229
<v Tomasz Nowak>Don't start. I've only just stopped being annoyed about it.</v>

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.770
<v Jamie Brennan>You're coming through twice when you get excited. Teams clearly wants us all to suffer.</v>

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get the full match report—what's already finished?</v>

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:56.880
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, finished the repair on the Gas Turbine 2 last night.</v>

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:00.700
<v Sarah Okafor>That's complete, not something carrying into this shift?</v>

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.920
<v Callum Reid>Complete. Just giving you the handover, no outstanding repair on that.</v>

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:11.819
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I finished the repair on the old turbine last night.</v>

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.500
<v David Whitfield>That was the repair we'd been carrying over?</v>

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.180
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the one. Finished, not another go at it today.</v>

00:01:22.609 --> 00:01:26.109
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Both repairs closed, then. Anything else from the shift?</v>

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:35.829
<v Hannah Price>Only an observation: saw the pressure on the barrel on three dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:38.019 --> 00:01:40.469
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, it recovered without anyone changing anything?</v>

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:49.689
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, on its own. I'm not asking for an investigation off the back of that, just saying what I saw.</v>

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.099
<v Callum Reid>Right, useful context. Not a job request.</v>

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:56.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only.</v>

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:02.670
<v Tomasz Nowak>And the existing blocker hasn't moved: can't get to the Engel until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:06.310
<v Callum Reid>There's no agreed window for that at the minute.</v>

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:12.729
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. So it's still blocked, I'm not saying I'm getting onto it today.</v>

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, keeping that as blocked. Nothing new allocated there.</v>

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:25.479
<v Callum Reid>On the GT1 fuel valve, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:29.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Cal. That's the permit to work and isolation you're taking?</v>

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:34.639
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, both. I'll take that, straight away.</v>

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:40.550
<v David Whitfield>Not a valve replacement being added in there, just to be clear?</v>

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:46.169
<v Callum Reid>No, just the permit to work and isolation for the GT1 fuel valve.</v>

00:02:48.539 --> 00:02:49.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Safety critical, understood.</v>

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.939
<v Hannah Price>And I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller. It's urgent.</v>

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Pricey, you've got that sign-off.</v>

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.650
<v Hannah Price>Yep. That's a separate item from what Cal's just said, obviously.</v>

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:12.979
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, different kit. The two isolation conversations were starting to run together on the audio.</v>

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:16.870
<v Sarah Okafor>No worries, they're separate.</v>

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:26.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Pricey, can you swap the filter on the line 1 hydraulics this afternoon as well? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:28.409 --> 00:03:36.110
<v Hannah Price>No, sorry, I can't take that as well. I've got the urgent sign-off I've just committed to. The filter needs someone else.</v>

00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:46.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Stores—sorry, stores Jamie, can you take that instead? Swap the filter on the line 1 hydraulics this afternoon. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:53.870
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take it instead of Pricey. This afternoon, and I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:54.729 --> 00:03:59.629
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, talking over you—actual filter swap, not just getting the filter out of stores?</v>

00:04:01.949 --> 00:04:06.150
<v Jamie Brennan>Actual swap, yeah. I'll swap the filter on the line 1 hydraulics.</v>

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's with stores Jamie now, not Pricey.</v>

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:17.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Olu, can you schedule downtime for the hot bearing with production this morning? Normal priority.</v>

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.420
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll schedule that with production this morning. Normal priority, got it.</v>

00:04:22.899 --> 00:04:27.800
<v Callum Reid>That's arranging the downtime, not saying the bearing work itself is happening this morning?</v>

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:33.920
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. I'll schedule downtime for the hot bearing; we're not agreeing the repair timing here.</v>

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.930
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it. Thanks.</v>

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.310
<v Sarah Okafor>David Whitfield, can you replace the seals on the main isolation valve this afternoon?</v>

00:04:43.589 --> 00:04:47.790
<v David Whitfield>Yep, I'll replace the seals on the main isolation valve this afternoon.</v>

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.600
<v Jamie Brennan>And that's the main isolation valve, not the GT1 fuel valve from earlier?</v>

00:04:54.959 --> 00:05:00.560
<v David Whitfield>Correct. Separate valve, separate job. Easy enough to lose track when we're all talking at once.</v>

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:08.670
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll grease and check the bearings on the old turbine by 11am. No rush on that one.</v>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:17.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, and that's separate from the repair I finished last night. Just so it doesn't sound like that repair's still open.</v>

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:24.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. Repair's done. I'm only taking the grease and bearing check, by 11am, no rush.</v>

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:29.339
<v Callum Reid>Got you, Sarah. Two different things.</v>

00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:37.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Stores Jamie, can you order spare parts for the Site Water System tomorrow morning, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:44.410
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll order spare parts for the Site Water System tomorrow morning. Spare-minute job, understood.</v>

00:05:45.579 --> 00:05:49.079
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Ordering only, yeah? Not fitting anything being slipped into that?</v>

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Ordering only. That's all we're agreeing there.</v>

00:05:54.139 --> 00:06:04.639
<v Jamie Brennan>While we're on mine, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team next week. That's an 'if you've got a spare minute' one, not something to bump the other work.</v>

00:06:06.829 --> 00:06:11.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie. Organise the toolbox talk for the team next week, spare-minute priority.</v>

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:18.939
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep. And I mean organise it, not that we're holding the talk on this call.</v>

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, because the football analysis was already quite a long toolbox talk.</v>

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.389
<v Hannah Price>With absolutely no useful learning points.</v>

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>Plenty. Mainly about disappointment.</v>

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:40.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, lovely. Everything agreed, and the blocked item stays blocked. No mystery jobs hidden in the handover.</v>

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:42.319
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, everyone.</v>
